  Check("tests", "smoke-guard-headroom", "tests/e2e/smoke-guard-headroom.sh", List(), 60000),
  // The entry-point rule, frozen on all three lanes: 0/1/2 explicit `main()` calls mean 1/1/2 runs.
  // Cheap (six short runs) and it guards a divergence that was invisible for two days because the
  // doubled block looked like the user's own file.
  Check("tests", "entry-auto-invoke-once", "tests/e2e/entry-auto-invoke-once.sh", List(), 240000),  // ceiling raised 2026-08-14: costs 36.6s, was under 4x it (smoke-guard-headroom)
  // Under a second, and it covers the failure shape that cost a user a binary they could not
  // rebuild: the Rust backend emitting a crate MISSING an imported def, leaving rustc to blame
  // their own call site. Both directions -- both import forms must REACH the crate, and what the
  // backend cannot lower must be a refusal that NAMES the def. Uses emit-rust, so no cargo.
  // 180s, from measurement rather than from taste: 55.9-74.8 s standalone depending on host load,
  // against a 60 s guard it TIMED OUT on twice. It runs five cargo builds (one pulling serde_json)
  // because the semantic half compiles and RUNS the emitted crates — emission alone would not have
  // caught the contract mismatch where `jsonParse` returned a String on this lane and a value on
