  // under a second. It also guards the escape hatch — SSC_STACKTRACE=1 must still produce frames,
  // or the "fix" would just be deleting the diagnostics.
  // 180s: measured 83.6 s standalone — over its old 60 s guard even on an idle host, which is why
  // it timed out rather than failed. Six JVM launches (both launchers x error/trace/working), and
  // a JVM start is ~10 s here.
  Check("tests", "cli-errors-are-messages", "tests/e2e/cli-errors-are-messages.sh", List(), 180000),
  // The sbt plugin is a SEPARATE build -- not in the root aggregate, not in ci.yml -- so its ten
  // scripted scenarios were run by nothing at all. That is how 1fea89a79 (a JS commit) deleted all
  // four of their .ssc-artifacts fixtures and nobody noticed for three weeks, leaving two scenarios
  // red and `identity` GREEN while it observed generation being skipped rather than emitting
  // nothing. Minutes here, against a suite that was decorative.
  // 600000: ten scenarios, each booting its own sbt and resolving Scala 2.12 for the plugin.
  // `ssc new` must produce a project that LOADS. It did not: five of six templates scaffold an
  // addSbtPlugin line for an artifact nobody published, so every generated project died on its
  // first sbt command with "Not found". Nothing had ever scaffolded a project and then tried to
  // build it, and inspecting the template FILES would not have caught it either — the coordinate
  // was well-formed, it just named something that did not exist. This resolves for real.
  // 300000: one `sbt update` in a scratch project, plus sbt's own boot.
  // Sub-second, and it guards a string that ends up in SOMEBODY ELSE's build file. The coordinate
  // `ssc` emits into a generated project must name a published release; a -SNAPSHOT there resolves
  // nowhere and fails at the user's first compile, in a file we wrote for them. Its only previous
  // protection was a comment saying "must track ThisBuild / version" -- which became actively wrong
  // the moment main moved to 0.2.0-SNAPSHOT after v0.1.0 shipped.
  Check("tests", "emitted-coordinate-is-published", "tests/e2e/emitted-coordinate-is-published.sh", List(), 60000),
  // The same shape one step further out: that gate guards a coordinate we write into somebody's
  // build, this one guards the COMMANDS we tell them to run. `releases/install.sh` downloaded an
